WEBVTT

00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:14,930
So, you know, there's a lot of studies that probably, you know, we think, though, we're

00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:18,690
going to take probiotics and we're going to change our gut, and that's really going

00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:19,690
to help my gut.

00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:20,690
It can be beneficial.

00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:25,370
I'm not saying that, but if you think you're going to re-floorize your gut, you think you're

00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:31,490
going to build your microbiota by simply taking probiotics, you missed the point.

00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:38,290
You build your microbiota and your microbiota changes quite quickly with the foods that you

00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:39,290
eat.

00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:46,010
You go on a vacation, everybody's probably experienced this and your diet changes, you know, drastically

00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:52,090
because you're on a vacation, you can be constipated for two days because your microbiota

00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:54,930
is just completely thrown in a loop.

00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:59,150
You go home, you get back on your regular diet and it seems to settle down and everything

00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:04,050
calms down instantly, your microbiota changes quickly.

00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:09,930
So, but it changes due to the foods that you eat.

00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:15,050
What is the worst habits that we could get into as Americans because we could go to the

00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:17,410
grocery store and get anything we want?

00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:22,090
We tend to have a habit of eating the same thing all the time.

00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:30,570
And even if it's something good for us, the lack of variety in our diet really affects the

00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:32,690
diversity of our microbiota.

00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:38,850
There's been plenty of studies that the diversity in our microbiota is based upon the diversity

00:01:38,850 --> 00:01:42,210
of different foods in our diet.

00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:49,650
So it is a catch-22 for a number of people that have, you know, really damaged, gotten borders.

00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:55,930
And they have antibodies to all sorts of different dietary proteins so they're limited to their

00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:56,930
diet.

00:01:56,930 --> 00:02:02,090
It's a difficult catch-22 to healing those people because if you want to diversify your

00:02:02,090 --> 00:02:05,610
microbiota, you have to diversify your food.

00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:10,330
So, eat as many different vegetables as possible.

00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:17,090
I know we tend to, we eat corn and beans and potatoes every night.

00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:23,090
Okay, that's not good, of course, or corn as a grade, but that's not part of the discussion.

00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:27,890
You know, if you're not, if you're eating the same thing all the time, that's not really good

00:02:27,890 --> 00:02:28,890
for your gut.

00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:38,690
So, if you want the healthy, diverse microbiota, you want as diverse a diet as possible, meaning

00:02:38,690 --> 00:02:42,650
as many different types of vegetables as possible.

00:02:42,650 --> 00:02:47,850
Different meats, different things in your diet, different fruits, not just the same thing

00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:48,850
all the time.

00:02:48,850 --> 00:02:56,890
And again, I've said this over and over over the years, so, you know, the danger of our grocery

00:02:56,890 --> 00:03:03,130
store habits these days is you could go and buy apples any time of the year.

00:03:03,130 --> 00:03:07,970
And I'm not saying apples are bad for him to say that, you know, I think we're supposed

00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:12,850
to eat things in season and our diets are supposed to rotate and change a lot.

00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:18,730
Because I think our microbiota is supposed to change and be diverse and that's how we protect

00:03:18,730 --> 00:03:26,090
against things like we talked about earlier, like an H. Polona infection, where you just

00:03:26,090 --> 00:03:31,730
have one rogue bacteria that goes wild and causes all sorts of disease.

